    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the welcome-notification side-effect for successful owner creation.\n\n**What the spec required:** on a successful create, emit a line via the logger named `NOTIFY` containing the owner id and the memberId.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **New component** `rest/controller/v1/WelcomeNotifier.java` \u2014 a `@Component` mirroring the existing `OwnerCreationAuditor` pattern. It logs to a dedicated `NOTIFY` logger via `enqueueWelcome(Owner)`, emitting `welcome owner id={} memberId={}` with the owner's id and assigned member id. Keeping the concern in its own class keeps the controller a thin entry point, consistent with how the audit concern is already factored out.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 injected the `WelcomeNotifier` via the constructor and invoked `welcomeNotifier.enqueueWelcome(owner)` in `createNewOwner`, right after the save/audit step (so it only fires on the successful `201 Created` path, after the member id is assigned).\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` test \u2014 which captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts a line contains both the owner id and the memberId \u2014 passes, and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The observed log line confirms it: `NOTIFY - welcome owner id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`.",
